# /etc/conf/modreg.d/s5 -- the defaults of the s5 filesystem module the
# kernel package carries (amix-dlm C2-3 v8 sec 1, C3-5 sec 1.2): one
# `param <name>=<value>` per default other than the module's own, `disable`
# to ship it off.  None: the module keeps its own defaults (probe=0).  The
# module is core tier, built with this kernel's cut, and is replaced with
# the kernel.  Local settings belong in /etc/conf/modreg.local.d/s5, which
# no package owns; then kbootset build and commit.
